To facilitate accurate marking, your submitted solution must use this template.

To complete each part of the exercise, add your own code to the following files:
part1: nothing to do, this solution is provided (stopwatch.c)
part2: nothing to do, this solution is provided (stopwatch.c)
part3: part3.c
part4: part4.c
additional part (optional): your own .c file(s) in the partAdditional folder


Please test your solution using the provided runall.sh script:
part1: ./runall.sh 1
part2: ./runall.sh 2
part3: ./runall.sh 3
part4: ./runall.sh 4
additional part: ./runall.sh additional


ADDITIONAL PART (optional, 1 mark)
Take your part 3 or part 4 program and add something new to it.
The partAdditional folder starts empty. This is where your additional part goes.

1. Put your .c file(s) in partAdditional. Any file name is fine.
   Start from a copy of your part 3 or part 4 code and change it.

2. Keep only your changed version in this folder.
   Do not also put your original part 3 or part 4 code in here.
   Only one program in this folder gets run.

3. You do not need to write a Makefile. The one in the folder finds your files by itself.
   A file with main() is built and run as a program.
   A file with module_init is built and loaded as a kernel module.
   Use one program, one kernel module, or one of each.

4. Header files go in the include folder, not in partAdditional.
   Include them like this:
       #include "../include/address_map_arm.h"

5. Test it with ./runall.sh additional
   This loads your kernel module first (if you have one).
   Then it loads the part 2 stopwatch driver (/dev/stopwatch).
   If your own module already makes /dev/stopwatch, the part 2 driver is skipped.
   Then it loads the built in KEY, SW and LEDR drivers and runs your program.
   To see what your module prints with printk, run: dmesg | tail

6. Fill in the ADDITIONAL PART section at the bottom of this README.
   I'll use it to find and test your work, so be specific.


To clean all directories and remove all drivers: ./runall clean


To submit your solution: ./runall.sh submit 
The script generates a .tar.bz2 archive. Please upload this
archive to quercus (only one team member needs to do this).


The script may generate errors, for example:
ERROR: Removing 'timer': No such file or directory
These errors can be ignored.


If you would like to clarify your interpretation of the exercise instructions 
or provide any additional information to the grader, PLEASE TYPE IT HERE:



